# Poll — options with vote bars, one vote per actor. A post's poll attachment:
# while the reader has not voted, each option is a button; the moment they have,
# every option in the SAME poll switches to a result bar, because a poll that
# still asked the reader to pick after they picked would be lying to them.
#
#     use Poll():
#         for o in PollOption where o.poll == t.id by id asc:
#             use PollOption(o.id, o.label, o.votes,
#                            sum(x.votes in PollOption where x.poll == t.id),
#                            exists(v in Vote where v.poll == t.id && v.voter == actor))
#         use PollFooter(sum(x.votes in PollOption where x.poll == t.id), "")
#
# ── `voted` IS ONE BOOLEAN FOR THE WHOLE POLL, NOT PER OPTION ─────────────────
#
# The library has no entity named `PollOption` or `Vote` — the host's does, with
# whatever name it chose — so the query that decides "has this actor already
# voted in THIS poll" cannot live here, the same reason `social/ThreadView`
# takes its reply count as a parameter rather than counting a `Reply` this file
# does not own. `exists(...)` is the right call for it, the same technique
# `FollowButton`'s and `SubscribeButton`'s doc comments already name: a query
# the HOST writes once and hands down as a plain `bool`. Every `PollOption` in
# one poll is called with the same value, because voting is a single event
# against the poll, not one against each option — the reader picked ONE row, and
# every option's presentation has to agree with that fact at once. Passing a
# different boolean per option (say, "did they vote for THIS one") could not
# distinguish "voted for something else" from "has not voted yet", and a poll
# that cannot tell those apart shows buttons to someone who already answered.
#
# ── THE BAR IS `ui/ProgressBar`, NOT A NEW BAR ────────────────────────────────
#
# A result is a label, a count and a total, which is exactly `ProgressBar`'s
# contract — this file draws no fill of its own and carries no width-class
# vocabulary, because `ui/progress.fct` already ships one and a second copy of
# fifty-one width rules for the same 2%-resolution bar is not a trade this
# library makes twice.
#
# ── THE VOTE ITSELF IS THE HOST'S FIXED `vote(option)` ACTION ─────────────────
# Named the same way `like`, `repost` and `bookmark` are on `EngagementBar`: a
# component parameter cannot forward a client cell's worth of context AND stay
# reusable across every poll on a page, so the option's own row id is the one
# argument the button needs, and `vote(id)` is the host action every poll on the
# page calls.
import "../ui/progress.fct"
app FacetSocial:
    css:
        [data-fa-mount] .x-poll { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px;
                   border: 1px solid var(--x-line, #2f3336); border-radius: var(--fa-radius, 16px);
                   padding: 12px 14px; margin-top: 8px; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-poll-opt-btn { display: block; width: 100%; text-align: left;
                       padding: 10px 14px; border: 1px solid var(--x-line, #2f3336);
                       border-radius: 9999px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600;
                       background: none; color: var(--fa-fg); cursor: pointer; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-poll-opt-btn:hover { border-color: var(--fa-accent);
                       background: var(--x-hover, rgba(239,243,244,.06)); }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-poll .x-progress-label { font-size: 14px; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-poll-foot { color: var(--fa-muted); font-size: 13px; }
    component Poll():
        box class "x-poll":
            slot
    component PollOption(id: int, label: text, votes: int, total: int, voted: bool):
        if !voted:
            button "{label}" -> vote(id) class "x-poll-opt-btn"
        if voted:
            use ProgressBar(label, votes, total)
    # The line under the options: the total and, when the host has one, when the
    # poll closes ("Final results", "Closes in 2h"). `closesLabel` is text and not
    # a timestamp for the same reason `profile/ProfileHeader`'s `joined` is: the
    # host owns the phrasing, this file only owns where it sits.
    component PollFooter(total: int, closesLabel: text):
        row class "x-poll-foot":
            text "{commas(total)} votes"
            if closesLabel != "":
                text "· {closesLabel}"
